MAJOR_VERSION=4
STANDARD_VERSION=5
RELEASE_VERSION=4
DESCRIPTION=Browser lab chat no longer duplicates messages: BroadcastChannel connect is single-flight, and the sender's line is appended once. Visitors on the published lab auto-join a shared WebSocket room (Cloudflare Durable Object on flintstone.bailey-forbes.com, with a CORS /relay-health probe) so multiple people can talk; if the hub is down the page falls back to same-origin BroadcastChannel. Switch user, register user, and Guest commands send paced QMP keys one shell line at a time (waiting for SWITCHUSER / Password / ok) and a connected relay seat follows the new principal after switchuser. The default lab boots a sandboxed Emscripten Flinstone Shell (make wasm / GitHub Action) so operators type at shell>; su, useradd, sessions, and server chat map onto the same identity and relay. The WASM page shows Flinstone Shell only (no duplicate kernel serial panel). Decorative macOS traffic-light close/minimize/zoom dots are removed from the titlebar. QEMU Wasm remains on ?qemu=1 and ?validate=1. Browser boot Playwright reads guest output from Flinstone Shell or COM1 and sends the guest chat line through Guest commands.

RELEASE_DATE=2026-09-15
